.TH HD-BASE 7 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-base \- the hyprdebian base system
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B hd-base
depends on the packages that every hyprdebian system has, so that they are
installed with it and stay installed.
Besides the settings below, a package it pulls in is set up the way that
package does it.
.PP
It holds the parts that every hyprdebian system shares, each with a man page
of its own:
.TP
.BR hd-config (7)
The hyprdebian configuration,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
where hyprdebian packages keep their settings under a key of their own, and
the configuration of each user in
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json ,
with
.BR hd-config-update (1)
and
.BR hd-config-remove (1).
.TP
.BR hd-network (7)
The network configuration:
.BR hd-network-render (8)
renders the
.BR systemd-networkd (8)
files from the key
.BR hd-network ,
in which
.BR hd-network-iface (8)
and
.BR hd-network-bridge (8)
change the interfaces and bridges, and the
.I .link
files that name ethernet and wifi interfaces by their path.
.TP
.BR hd-secboot (7)
The Secure Boot keys of the owner, which the postinst generates in
.I /etc/hyprdebian/secboot
with
.BR hd-secboot (8)
when they are not there yet; it also writes them in the firmware and turns
Secure Boot on and off.
.PP
It installs
.BR hd-up (1),
which upgrades the system after a ZFS snapshot, by hand and every week with
.BR hd-up.timer ,
.BR hd-reboot-check (1),
which tells whether a reboot is needed, as after a new kernel,
.BR hd-reboot (1)
and
.BR hd-poweroff (1),
which reboot and power off the system with
.B hyprshutdown
in a Hyprland session and with
.B systemctl
otherwise,
.BR hd-link-repo (8),
which switches the HyprDebian repository and suite of apt,
.BR hd-firmware (8),
which finds and installs the firmware packages that the hardware needs, and
the files
that new users
get in their home directory, from
.IR /etc/skel ,
with
.BR hd-sync-skel (1),
which brings them into an existing home directory:
.TP
.I .bash_aliases
.B ls
and
.B ll
with
.BR eza (1),
.B y
for
.BR yazi (1),
.B wav2flac
which converts the
.I .wav
files below the current folder to
.I .flac
with
.BR ffmpeg (1)
and deletes them, and a history search on Ctrl-R with
.BR fzf (1).
.TP
.I .config/nano/nanorc
Indents with four spaces, remembers the search history, and colors the
interface and the syntax.
.PP
It also sets up the system:
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/local\-bin\-path.sh
Adds
.I ~/.local/bin
to the
.B PATH
of login shells, when that folder exists.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/preferences.d/00\-block\-unwanted
Keeps apt from installing
.BR ifupdown ,
as
.BR systemd-networkd (8)
runs the network,
.BR os-prober ,
and
.BR turnstile .
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50hyprdebian\-languages
Keeps apt from downloading the translations of the package descriptions,
some 40 MB in
.IR /var/lib/apt/lists ;
that includes the English one, so
.B apt show
has no long descriptions.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50hyprdebian\-no\-recommends
Keeps apt from installing the recommends of a package, so the system only
gets what its packages depend on.
The hd-* packages depend on everything they need.
.TP
.I /etc/dpkg/dpkg.cfg.d/hyprdebian\-excludes
Has
.BR dpkg (1)
leave out of every package the documentation in
.I /usr/share/doc
but the copyright files, the translations in
.IR /usr/share/locale ,
the man pages in other languages
than English and the info pages.
The postinst removes these files from the packages that were installed
before it, on the first installation and on an upgrade from a version
before 1.26.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd\-zfs\-scrub.timer
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd\-zfs\-trim.timer
Scrub the ZFS pools on the second Sunday of the month and trim them on the
first, with the scripts of zfsutils-linux, as its cron job does on a system
with cron, which HyprDebian does not have.
A pool is left out when its property
.B org.debian:periodic\-scrub
or
.B org.debian:periodic\-trim
is
.BR disable ;
at the default,
.BR auto ,
only a pool that is only on NVMe disks is trimmed.
The timers are enabled on the first installation.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd\-up.timer
Runs
.B hd-up \-\-unattended
with
.B hd-up.service
every Tuesday at 04:30, or after the next boot when the system was off then,
except on battery power; see
.BR hd-up (1).
The timer is enabled on its first installation.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/getty@.service.d/numlock.conf
Turns Num Lock on for a console before its login prompt shows, with
.BR setleds (1).
.TP
.I /etc/update\-motd.d/00\-hyprdebian
Shows the HyprDebian banner after a login on the console or over ssh, with
the version of HyprDebian from
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/version.json ,
the suite and the Debian version, the kernel, the uptime, the load, the
memory, the health of the ZFS pools and the RAID arrays, the failed
units, and why a reboot is needed, as
.BR hd-reboot-check (1)
finds it.
.TP
.I /etc/kernel/postinst.d/zz\-hd\-reboot\-check
Runs
.B hd-reboot-check \-\-write
after a kernel is installed, so
.I /run/reboot-required
says that a reboot is due also when the kernel did not come with
.BR hd-up (1).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/zram\-generator.conf.d/hyprdebian.conf
A swap in compressed RAM,
.IR /dev/zram0 ,
of a quarter of the RAM, compressed with zstd, with priority 16384, so it is
used before the swap on disk; see
.BR zram-generator.conf (5).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysctl.d/50\-zram.conf
Sets
.B vm.swappiness
to 180, as swapping to zram is cheaper than dropping the page cache, and
.B vm.page\-cluster
to 0, as reading ahead does not help with zram.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/resolved.conf.d/00\-direct\-uplink.conf
Has
.BR systemd-resolved (8)
pass the queries straight to the name servers of the network: no stub
resolver on 127.0.0.53, no cache, no LLMNR, no multicast DNS and no fallback
servers.
.PP
Services are enabled on their installation as on Debian, by their presets,
see
.BR systemd.preset (5).
.PP
The postinst masks
.BR systemd-firstboot.service ,
.B rpcbind.socket
and
.B rpcbind.service
on the first installation; a unit that the admin unmasks again stays
unmasked on upgrades, and a purge unmasks them.
An upgrade from a version before 1.1 unmasks
.B systemd-preset-all.service
and
.BR systemd-machine-id-commit.service ,
which those versions masked as well, and renames the apt source
.IR /etc/apt/sources.list.d/hyprdebian.local.sources ,
the name of versions before 1.11, to
.IR hyprdebian.sources .
It also points
.I /etc/resolv.conf
at
.IR /run/systemd/resolve/resolv.conf ,
the name servers themselves, in place of the stub resolver, when it is the
link that
.B systemd-resolved
made.
When that file is missing, because
.B systemd-resolved
does not run, as in the chroot of the installer, it is made with the name
servers of the old link, so names keep resolving until
.B systemd-resolved
starts.
It empties
.IR /etc/motd ,
on the first installation like the masks, and diverts
.I /etc/update\-motd.d/10\-uname
of base-files to
.IR 10\-uname.base\-files ,
which
.BR run-parts (8)
skips, as the banner already shows the kernel; a removal of the package
puts it back.
It diverts
.I /etc/issue
of base-files to
.I /etc/issue.debian
and has
.BR hd-issue (8)
write the HyprDebian login banner there, with the version, the type and the
suite, on every installation and upgrade; a removal of the package puts the
banner of base-files back.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/version.json
The version of HyprDebian, as
.B {"major": 1, "minor": 0}
for 1.0, which is also the version of
.BR hd-base .
The banners show it.
.SH PACKAGES
The installer starts from the minimal base of Debian, the
.B minbase
variant of
.BR debootstrap (8),
so these are all the packages besides the required ones of Debian.
.TP
.B hyprdebian
.B python3
and
.BR sudo ,
for
.BR hd-up (1);
.BR python3-jinja2 ,
for
.BR hd-link-repo (8)
and
.BR hd-network-render (8);
.BR kbd ,
for Num Lock on the console;
.BR kmod ,
for
.BR hd-firmware (8).
.TP
.B Init
.BR systemd ,
.B systemd-sysv
and
.BR udev .
.TP
.B Secure Boot
.BR openssl ,
.B efitools
and
.BR sbsigntool ,
which make the keys, enroll them and sign EFI files with them; see
.BR hd-secboot (7).
.TP
.B Remote access and firewall
.B openssh-server
and
.BR openssh-client ,
the ssh server and client, which openssh-server no longer pulls in;
.BR kitty-terminfo ,
so that the kitty terminal works over ssh;
.BR ufw ,
the firewall.
.TP
.B Network
.B iproute2
and
.BR iputils-ping ,
with
.BR linux-sysctl-defaults ,
which lets every user ping;
.BR netbase .
.TP
.B ZFS
.BR zfs-dkms ,
.B zfsutils-linux
and
.BR zfs-initramfs ;
.BR zfs-zed ,
the event daemon that reports pool errors, resilvers and scrubs;
.B initramfs-tools
for the initrd, and
.B zstd
to compress it.
DKMS builds the ZFS module with the compiler that the kernel headers bring
along.
.TP
.B Boot
.B efibootmgr
for the boot entries of the firmware.
.TP
.B Console
.BR locales ,
.BR keyboard-configuration ,
.B console-setup
and
.BR ca-certificates ;
.BR whiptail ,
which shows the debconf questions in dialogs.
.TP
.B System services
.BR systemd-resolved ,
name resolution;
.B libpam-systemd
and
.BR libnss-systemd ,
which register every login as a session of
.BR systemd-logind (8),
with its runtime directory and the user instance of systemd.
The logs stay in the journal of
.BR systemd-journald (8);
there is no syslog daemon.
.TP
.B Command line tools
.BR nano ,
.BR less ,
.BR procps ,
.BR eza ,
.BR fzf ,
.BR psmisc ,
.BR bash-completion ,
.BR command-not-found ,
.BR man-db ,
.B apt-file
and
.BR systemd-zram-generator .
It conflicts with
.BR zram-tools ,
which would set up a second zram swap.
It replaces
.BR hd-config ,
.B hd-network
and
.BR hd-secboot ,
the packages that held the configuration, the network configuration and
the Secure Boot keys before; an upgrade removes them, and the configuration
and the keys stay.
.PP
The firmware is not among them: each system needs other firmware, which
.BR hd-firmware (8)
finds from its hardware and installs.
Most of it is in the
.B non-free-firmware
component of Debian, which the apt sources must include.
On an upgrade from a version before 1.23, which depended on all of the
firmware, run
.B hd-firmware \-\-install
before
.BR "apt autoremove" ,
so the firmware the hardware needs stays installed.
.PP
Versions before 1.26 also depended on
.BR build-essential ,
.BR git ,
.BR git-delta ,
.BR nfs-common ,
.BR net-tools ,
.BR pciutils ,
.BR usbutils ,
.B acpi
and
.BR ack .
After an upgrade
.B apt autoremove
removes them; mark the ones that are still used as installed by hand
first, such as
.B apt-mark manual nfs-common
on a system that mounts NFS shares.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-up
Upgrades the system after a ZFS snapshot.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-reboot-check
Tells whether a reboot is needed.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-reboot
.TQ
.I /usr/bin/hd-poweroff
Reboot and power off the system.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-sync-skel
Brings the files of
.I /etc/skel
into the home directory.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-config-update
.TQ
.I /usr/bin/hd-config-remove
Change the hyprdebian configuration: of the system for root, of the user for
other users.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-issue
Writes the login banner in
.IR /etc/issue .
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-link-repo
Switches the HyprDebian repository and suite of apt.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-network-render
.TQ
.I /usr/sbin/hd-network-iface
.TQ
.I /usr/sbin/hd-network-bridge
Render and change the network configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-secboot
Generates the Secure Boot keys, writes them in the firmware and turns Secure
Boot on and off.
.TP
.I /usr/sbin/hd-firmware
Finds and installs the firmware packages that the hardware needs.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The hyprdebian configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/secboot
The Secure Boot keys.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-base/templates/hyprdebian.sources.j2
The template of the apt source of
.BR hd-link-repo .
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/version.json
The version of HyprDebian, a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/skel/.bash_aliases
.TQ
.I /etc/skel/.config/nano/nanorc
The files new users get, conffiles.
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/local\-bin\-path.sh
Adds
.I ~/.local/bin
to the
.BR PATH ,
a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/preferences.d/00\-block\-unwanted
The packages apt never installs, a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50hyprdebian\-languages
No translations of the package descriptions, a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/50hyprdebian\-no\-recommends
No recommends, a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/dpkg/dpkg.cfg.d/hyprdebian\-excludes
The files dpkg leaves out, a conffile.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd\-zfs\-scrub.timer
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd\-zfs\-trim.timer
The monthly scrub and trim of the ZFS pools, with their services.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd\-up.timer
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/hd\-up.service
The weekly unattended upgrade.
.TP
.I /etc/update\-motd.d/00\-hyprdebian
The banner after a login, a conffile.
.TP
.I /etc/kernel/postinst.d/zz\-hd\-reboot\-check
Writes
.I /run/reboot-required
after a kernel is installed, a conffile.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/getty@.service.d/numlock.conf
Num Lock on the console.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/zram\-generator.conf.d/hyprdebian.conf
The zram swap.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysctl.d/50\-zram.conf
The sysctls for the zram swap.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/resolved.conf.d/00\-direct\-uplink.conf
The config of systemd-resolved.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/10\-ethernet.link
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/20\-wifi.link
Name the network interfaces by their path.
